    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92309.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "I was a little kid and got to know him. I was excited when he met this wonderful teacher in town named Carol, and they got engaged and married, and then started having these couple of wonderful kids, Sarah and Eric, and it was just fun to watch you grow up, and your family's always was such an important influence in the Harrisonville community. And lo and behold, in 1994, when I was asked to run for state representative, I was looking for a campaign treasurer and someone recommended your father because he had served in the state legislature at one time and so I still remember the evening I went by and sat down and visited with him and he was gracious enough to agree to be my campaign manager or treasurer and he was just such a wonderful friend to me and a help and of course we won that campaign and went on and served six years in the Missouri legislature. And it was just fun to continue on that friendship with you and your family and watch you graduate from college and go on to great things graduating from law school. And then when I ran for Congress and won, to be contacted with you and have this discussion about maybe you coming and moving from Missouri to come out to Washington DC with me and serve as my legislative director and you did and brought your beautiful wife Sarah and It was just great to have you there as part of the team heart slur as we've put together our office and started serving the Missouri Fourth District and then very soon became my chief of staff. I was very blessed to have you helping lead my whole team for five years. Now I'm just so proud of you and your new role here with Farm Bureau. know that you're just going to be a fantastic asset to this organization and states and couldn't be more proud of you.",
