  {
    "episode_id": 92309,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92309.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "It really was. When I was asked to run for Congress, I studied the map of the 4th congressional district because I wasn't really sure totally of the 24 counties which ones were in and not. And then I had to think of this daunting task of trying to campaign in such a large area. And you do need people in every county willing to help put up signs and to advocate for you and that's tough. And the first people that I thought of was Farm Bureau friends because I, through Missouri Farm Bureau, had met other people in other counties and it was wonderful to call them and all of them that I visited with and said, would you help me out say, absolutely we will. And it was very critical to helping me win. And now it's such an honor to partner with them to bring a first-hand experience of agriculture to Washington.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
