    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92309.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "Right. I was a home economics teacher for 11 years before I was asked to run for state representatives. Now they call it family and consumer sciences or fax teacher. And so I think my background dealing with nutrition certainly is helpful as well as dealing with students of all income backgrounds and working with individuals who maybe help utilize the food stamp program. The usage of the food stamps program was just skyrocketing until recently the change of the economy has now caused the usage to start going down. But there was a point when one out of every six Americans was on food stamps a few years ago. And I think there's a real need to start looking at that whole program because we want to help people who truly need it. But we want to make sure that it's just a temporary thing that we help people get back working again where they don't need this assistance. And that's where some changes I think will take place to try to reduce some of the fraud and incentivize people to get back to work if they're able to physically.",
